---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
import { SITE } from '../../lib/site';
---
<Base title="Privacy notice" description="How Ukraine Medical Admissions collects, uses, stores and protects personal information from enquiries and applications.">
  <div class="page-head"><div class="wrap"><span class="eyebrow">Legal</span><h1>Privacy notice</h1><p>Draft for legal review — effective date to be set before publication.</p></div></div>
  <Breadcrumbs items={[{ label: 'Privacy' }]} />
  <section style="padding-top:1rem"><div class="wrap prose">
    <h2>Who we are</h2>
    <p>Ukraine Medical Admissions (“we”) operates {SITE.url}. Contact: <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a>. [Legal entity name, registered address and country to be inserted.]</p>
    <h2>What we collect and why</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Enquiries (contact form):</strong> name, email and your message. Used to reply to you. Legal basis: your consent and steps taken at your request before any contract.</li>
      <li><strong>Candidate profiles (the application form, stage 1):</strong> your name and email; your study plans (field of study, level, preferred universities and preferred start); your education history (highest level, qualification, awarding country, year, grading scale, and the subjects and grades you choose to enter, including results still outstanding); which documents you say you have, still need or are not sure about (we do not collect the documents themselves at this stage); the country where you live; your nationality, if you choose to give it; your preferred language for our emails; and your questions. Used to reply to you and to compare what you told us with the published requirements of the universities you name. Legal basis: your consent and steps taken at your request before any contract.</li>
      <li><strong>Applications (when the secure dashboard is available):</strong> identity and academic documents you choose to upload. Used solely to prepare and, with your explicit confirmation, submit your application to the university. These are stored outside public web directories, access-controlled and retained only as long as needed.</li>
      <li><strong>Website analytics:</strong> none installed. We use no analytics or advertising trackers today; if we add privacy-respecting measurement, this notice will name the tool before it is switched on.</li>
    </ul>
    <h2>Sharing</h2>
    <p>We share your information with a university only when you confirm an official submission. We do not sell personal data and we do not use it for advertising.</p>
    <h2>Retention</h2>
    <p>Enquiries: up to 12 months after our last contact. Application records and documents: for the duration of the application process and a limited period afterwards for accountability, then securely deleted. [Exact periods to be confirmed.]</p>
    <h2>Your rights</h2>
    <p>You can ask for a copy of your data, correction, deletion, or restriction of processing, and withdraw consent at any time by emailing us. Where UK or EU data-protection law applies, you also have the right to complain to the relevant supervisory authority.</p>
    <h2>Security</h2>
    <p>We use encrypted connections (HTTPS), restrict access to personal data to people who need it, keep documents out of public web directories, and keep records of who accessed what.</p>
  </div></section>
</Base>
